<title>USA: N.Y. business loans fell $768 mln in April 9 wk.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans fell $768 mln in April 9 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, fell $768 million to $45,079 million in the week ended April 9, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans fell $777 million to $45,344 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $2,125 million to $840,554 billion.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
</text>
